{"title":"Career roadmap · Religious Studies Researcher","role":"Religious Studies Researcher","summary":"A Religious Studies Researcher investigates religions, religious texts, institutions, beliefs, practices, communities, history, philosophy, ethics, and the relationship between religion and society.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A Religious Studies Researcher investigates religions, religious texts, institutions, beliefs, practices, communities, history, philosophy, ethics, and the relationship between religion and society."},{"type":"p","text":"This pathway can support research in universities, think tanks, museums, archives, cultural institutions, NGOs, interfaith organisations, publishing, policy organisations, and international research bodies."},{"type":"p","text":"The most important distinction is between academic study of religion and religious ministry. A researcher studies religion using scholarly methods and does not need to personally practise the religion being studied."},{"type":"p","text":"For this degree, the strongest profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Religious Studies","Research Methods","Language/Textual Skills","History","Sociology/Anthropology","Digital Humanities"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Research Intern, Research Assistant"},{"text":"Literature review and data collection"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Junior Researcher, Research Associate"},{"text":"Religious/cultural research"}],[{"text":"Core Career"},{"text":"Religious Studies Researcher, Research Analyst"},{"text":"Independent research"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Research Fellow, Academic Researcher"},{"text":"Specialised research and publications"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Senior Research Fellow, Research Specialist"},{"text":"Research leadership"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Research Lead, Programme Director"},{"text":"Research programmes and teams"}],[{"text":"Academic"},{"text":"Lecturer/Professor/Research Professor*"},{"text":"Teaching and advanced research"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"*Academic positions normally require appropriate postgraduate and doctoral qualifications."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Foundations of Religion & Society"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Introduction to religious studies"},{"text":"Comparative religion"},{"text":"History of religions"},{"text":"Religious philosophy"},{"text":"Sociology of religion"},{"text":"Anthropology of religion"},{"text":"Psychology of religion"},{"text":"Religion and society"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Indian religious traditions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Comparative perspective"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Buddhism"},{"text":"Islam"},{"text":"Christianity"},{"text":"Jainism"},{"text":"Hindu traditions"},{"text":"Sikhism"},{"text":"Judaism"},{"text":"Other major world religions and indigenous traditions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is scholarly comparison rather than treating one tradition as the default standard for evaluating another."},{"type":"h","text":"Research skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic reading"},{"text":"Source evaluation"},{"text":"Citation"},{"text":"Note-taking"},{"text":"Literature searches"},{"text":"Academic writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Comparative Study of Religious Communities in India"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"History"},{"text":"Beliefs"},{"text":"Institutions"},{"text":"Social practices"},{"text":"Cultural contributions"},{"text":"Contemporary developments"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Research Methods & Textual Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from general knowledge toward systematic research."},{"type":"h","text":"Research methods"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Ethnographic methods"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Oral history"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Case studies"},{"text":"Content analysis"},{"text":"Discourse analysis"},{"text":"Comparative research"},{"text":"Archival research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Textual studies"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Textual criticism"},{"text":"Historical context"},{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Interpretation"},{"text":"Manuscript studies"},{"text":"Source criticism"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Language development"},{"type":"p","text":"A serious researcher should consider learning at least one relevant language beyond English."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sanskrit"},{"text":"Pali"},{"text":"Prakrit"},{"text":"Arabic"},{"text":"Persian"},{"text":"Urdu"},{"text":"Classical languages relevant to Christian studies"},{"text":"Regional Indian languages"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The choice should match the student's research tradition."},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Religious Texts and Their Historical Context"},{"type":"p","text":"Select a scholarly research question and compare primary and secondary sources."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Students should choose a research domain rather than remaining completely general."},{"type":"h","text":"1. Buddhist Studies"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Buddhist philosophy"},{"text":"Pali literature"},{"text":"Sanskrit Buddhist texts"},{"text":"Buddhist history"},{"text":"Buddhist art"},{"text":"Monastic traditions"},{"text":"Buddhist societies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Islamic Studies"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Islamic history"},{"text":"Qur'anic studies"},{"text":"Hadith studies"},{"text":"Islamic philosophy"},{"text":"Islamic law as an academic field"},{"text":"Sufism"},{"text":"Muslim societies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Christian Studies"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biblical studies"},{"text":"Early Christianity"},{"text":"Christian history"},{"text":"Theology as an academic subject"},{"text":"Christianity and society"},{"text":"Christian ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Jain Studies"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Jain philosophy"},{"text":"Prakrit texts"},{"text":"Jain history"},{"text":"Jain ethics"},{"text":"Jain art and manuscripts"},{"text":"Jain communities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Comparative Religion"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Comparative theology/religion"},{"text":"Interfaith relations"},{"text":"Religious pluralism"},{"text":"Religion and politics"},{"text":"Religion and society"},{"text":"Secularism"},{"text":"Religious identity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Religion & Society"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Anthropology"},{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Gender"},{"text":"Social change"},{"text":"Religion and development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"7. Religion & Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"An emerging area:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI and religion"},{"text":"Digital religion"},{"text":"Online religious communities"},{"text":"Religious misinformation"},{"text":"Technology ethics"},{"text":"Digital humanities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Independent Research"},{"type":"p","text":"For a 4-year Honours programme, develop an academic research profile."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research design"},{"text":"Literature synthesis"},{"text":"Primary-source research"},{"text":"Archival research"},{"text":"Fieldwork"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Academic publishing"},{"text":"Conference presentations"},{"text":"Research ethics"},{"text":"Grant/proposal writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Zotero"},{"text":"Mendeley"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"NVivo or equivalent qualitative-analysis tools"},{"text":"R/Python basics"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"OCR"},{"text":"Text analysis"},{"text":"Corpus analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"2–3 research papers"},{"text":"5–10 research briefs"},{"text":"1 major dissertation"},{"text":"Conference presentation"},{"text":"Primary-source analysis"},{"text":"Digital research project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Comparative Religion Research Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a research project combining:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Primary Sources","Historical Context","Textual Analysis","Comparative Framework","Data","Research Findings"]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible components:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Religious text database"},{"text":"Timeline"},{"text":"Geographic mapping"},{"text":"Bibliography"},{"text":"Citation network"},{"text":"Text search"},{"text":"Comparative analysis"},{"text":"Visualisations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project Ideas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Religion and Social Change in Contemporary India"},{"text":"Comparative Study of Buddhist, Jain and Hindu Ethical Traditions"},{"text":"Religion and Digital Communities"},{"text":"Religious Pluralism and Interfaith Relations"},{"text":"Migration and Religious Identity"},{"text":"Religion and Gender in Contemporary Society"},{"text":"Digital Preservation of Religious Manuscripts"},{"text":"Religion and Artificial Intelligence"},{"text":"Comparative Study of Religious Educational Traditions"},{"text":"Religion, Peacebuilding and Conflict Resolution"},{"text":"Religious Architecture and Cultural Heritage"},{"text":"Digital Humanities Approach to Religious Texts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4-Year Honours / Advanced Variant"},{"type":"p","text":"Specialise in one of the following:"},{"type":"h","text":"Textual Studies"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Manuscript studies"},{"text":"Textual criticism"},{"text":"Philology"},{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Historical linguistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Religion & Society"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Anthropology"},{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Religion and development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Philosophy & Ethics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Religious philosophy"},{"text":"Comparative ethics"},{"text":"Bioethics"},{"text":"Technology ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"History & Culture"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Religious history"},{"text":"Art"},{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"Heritage"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Interfaith Studies"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Religious pluralism"},{"text":"Dialogue"},{"text":"Peacebuilding"},{"text":"Conflict resolution"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Humanities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"Corpus analysis"},{"text":"NLP"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Knowledge graphs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation Options"},{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Possible Career"],"rows":[[{"text":"Buddhist Studies"},{"text":"Buddhist Studies Researcher"}],[{"text":"Islamic Studies"},{"text":"Islamic Studies Researcher"}],[{"text":"Christian Studies"},{"text":"Christian Studies Researcher"}],[{"text":"Jain Studies"},{"text":"Jain Studies Researcher"}],[{"text":"Comparative Religion"},{"text":"Comparative Religion Researcher"}],[{"text":"Religion & Society"},{"text":"Religion & Society Researcher"}],[{"text":"Religious History"},{"text":"Religious History Researcher"}],[{"text":"Religious Philosophy"},{"text":"Religion & Philosophy Researcher"}],[{"text":"Religious Texts"},{"text":"Textual Studies Researcher"}],[{"text":"Manuscript Studies"},{"text":"Manuscript Researcher"}],[{"text":"Religion & Heritage"},{"text":"Cultural Heritage Researcher"}],[{"text":"Interfaith Studies"},{"text":"Interfaith Programme Researcher"}],[{"text":"Digital Religion"},{"text":"Digital Religion Researcher"}],[{"text":"Religion & Technology"},{"text":"Religion & Technology Researcher"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core knowledge"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Religious studies"},{"text":"Comparative religion"},{"text":"Religious history"},{"text":"Philosophy"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Anthropology"},{"text":"Ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Ethnography"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Archival research"},{"text":"Content analysis"},{"text":"Discourse analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Textual"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Source criticism"},{"text":"Textual criticism"},{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Manuscript studies"},{"text":"Philology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Languages"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop at least one research-relevant language:"},{"type":"p","text":"Sanskrit / Pali / Prakrit / Arabic / Persian / Urdu / relevant classical or regional language"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Zotero/Mendeley"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"NVivo"},{"text":"R/Python"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"OCR"},{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"Corpus analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Communication"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Conference presentations"},{"text":"Research proposals"},{"text":"Policy/research briefs"},{"text":"Teaching"},{"text":"Public communication"}]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Universities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Religious Studies departments"},{"text":"Philosophy departments"},{"text":"History departments"},{"text":"Sociology/Anthropology departments"},{"text":"Digital Humanities labs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cultural institutions"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Museums"},{"text":"Archives"},{"text":"Manuscript libraries"},{"text":"Heritage organisations"},{"text":"Cultural research centres"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research organisations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"Social research institutes"},{"text":"Interfaith organisations"},{"text":"Peace and conflict organisations"},{"text":"Public policy institutions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"NGOs"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Community development"},{"text":"Interfaith dialogue"},{"text":"Peacebuilding"},{"text":"Human rights"},{"text":"Cultural preservation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Deliverables"},{"type":"p","text":"Aim to produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Research report"},{"text":"Interview study"},{"text":"Archival catalogue"},{"text":"Religious text analysis"},{"text":"Survey dataset"},{"text":"Research dashboard"},{"text":"Policy/research brief"},{"text":"Conference presentation"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative methods"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Academic publishing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital humanities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"Text analysis"},{"text":"OCR"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Digital preservation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Python/R"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Language"},{"type":"p","text":"Formal or university-level study in a research language can be more valuable than generic certificates."},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital humanities"},{"text":"Computational text analysis"},{"text":"NLP"},{"text":"AI-assisted research"},{"text":"Knowledge graphs"}]}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Entry-level"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Documentation Assistant"},{"text":"Project Assistant"},{"text":"Cultural Research Assistant"},{"text":"Archive Assistant"},{"text":"Programme Assistant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Junior Researcher"},{"text":"Research Associate"},{"text":"Research Analyst"},{"text":"Religious Studies Researcher"},{"text":"Cultural Researcher"},{"text":"Social Researcher"},{"text":"Research Coordinator"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Buddhist Studies Researcher"},{"text":"Islamic Studies Researcher"},{"text":"Christian Studies Researcher"},{"text":"Jain Studies Researcher"},{"text":"Comparative Religion Researcher"},{"text":"Religious History Researcher"},{"text":"Textual Researcher"},{"text":"Digital Humanities Researcher"},{"text":"Religion & Society Researcher"},{"text":"Interfaith Researcher"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research Fellow"},{"text":"Senior Research Fellow"},{"text":"Research Programme Lead"},{"text":"Academic Researcher"},{"text":"Research Director"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Academic teaching and senior university research positions generally require postgraduate and doctoral qualifications."},{"type":"h","text":"What Employers / Research Institutions May Test"},{"type":"h","text":"Research design"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a research methodology for studying changing religious practices among young adults."},{"type":"h","text":"Source criticism"},{"type":"p","text":"How would you assess whether a historical religious source is reliable?"},{"type":"h","text":"Comparative research"},{"type":"p","text":"How would you compare two religious traditions without imposing the assumptions of one tradition onto the other?"},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative research"},{"type":"p","text":"Design an interview study examining religious identity."},{"type":"h","text":"Textual analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"How would you analyse a primary religious text within its historical context?"},{"type":"h","text":"Ethics"},{"type":"p","text":"What ethical issues arise when researching people's religious beliefs?"},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse survey data on religious participation and identify significant patterns."},{"type":"h","text":"Writing"},{"type":"p","text":"Produce a 500-word evidence-based research brief from multiple academic sources."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For serious research careers, postgraduate education is highly recommended."},{"type":"h","text":"Religious Studies"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Religious Studies"},{"text":"MA Comparative Religion"},{"text":"MA Religion/Philosophy"},{"text":"MA Interfaith Studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tradition-specific"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Buddhist Studies"},{"text":"Islamic Studies"},{"text":"Christian Studies"},{"text":"Jain Studies"},{"text":"Sanskrit/Pali/Arabic/Persian studies as relevant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Interdisciplinary"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA History"},{"text":"MA Sociology"},{"text":"MA Anthropology"},{"text":"MA Philosophy"},{"text":"MA Cultural Studies"},{"text":"MA Peace & Conflict Studies"},{"text":"MA Heritage Studies"},{"text":"MA Public Policy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MA / Master's","Research Assistant / Project Researcher","PhD","Research Fellow / Academic Researcher","Senior Researcher / Faculty / Research Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential master's areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Religious Studies"},{"text":"Comparative Religion"},{"text":"Theology/Religious Studies"},{"text":"Buddhist Studies"},{"text":"Islamic Studies"},{"text":"Christian Studies"},{"text":"Jain Studies"},{"text":"Anthropology of Religion"},{"text":"Sociology of Religion"},{"text":"Philosophy of Religion"},{"text":"Religion & Politics"},{"text":"Religion & Society"},{"text":"Peace & Conflict Studies"},{"text":"Digital Humanities"},{"text":"Manuscript Studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong combinations"},{"type":"h","text":"Religious Studies + Digital Humanities"},{"type":"h","text":"Religion + Anthropology"},{"type":"h","text":"Religion + Peace & Conflict"},{"type":"h","text":"Religion + Philosophy/Ethics"},{"type":"h","text":"Religious Texts + Computational Humanities"},{"type":"h","text":"Religion + Public Policy"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Research Intern","Research Assistant","Junior Researcher","Research Associate","Religious Studies Researcher","Research Fellow","Senior Research Fellow","Research Programme Lead","Research Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Academic route"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MA / Master's","MPhil/PhD or relevant doctoral route","Postdoctoral / Research Fellow","Lecturer / Assistant Professor*","Associate Professor","Professor / Research Chair"]},{"type":"p","text":"*Exact academic eligibility depends on country, institution, discipline, and current regulations."},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 Career Evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Religious Studies research is likely to increasingly intersect with digital humanities, computational linguistics, AI, migration, conflict studies, ethics, and digital communities."},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital Religion Researcher"},{"text":"Computational Religion Researcher"},{"text":"AI & Religion Researcher"},{"text":"Religion & Technology Ethics Researcher"},{"text":"Religious Text Data Analyst"},{"text":"Digital Humanities Researcher"},{"text":"Religious Heritage Data Specialist"},{"text":"Interfaith Policy Researcher"},{"text":"Religion & Geopolitics Analyst"},{"text":"Digital Manuscript Researcher"},{"text":"AI-Assisted Textual Research Specialist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Future research workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Primary Texts / Archives","Digitisation / OCR","Metadata","Text & Data Analysis","AI-Assisted Pattern Discovery","Human Scholarly Interpretation","Peer Review","Research Publication"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI can help researchers search large textual collections, translate material, identify patterns, organise references, and perform computational analysis. However, historical context, interpretation, source criticism, attribution, and scholarly judgement remain essential."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"flow","items":["Religious Studies","Comparative Religion","History","Philosophy"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Methodology","Qualitative/Quantitative Methods","Ethnography","Archival Research"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Textual"},{"type":"flow","items":["Source Criticism","Textual Analysis","Language Skills","Manuscript Studies"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"flow","items":["Digital Humanities","GIS","OCR","Corpus Analysis","Digital Archives"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","Statistics","Power BI","Python/R"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Communication"},{"type":"flow","items":["Academic Writing","Research Papers","Presentations","Research Proposals"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"flow","items":["NLP","Computational Text Analysis","Knowledge Graphs","AI-Assisted Research"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"0–2 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Intern","Research Assistant","Junior Researcher"]},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Associate","Religious Studies Researcher","Research Analyst"]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Fellow","Specialist Researcher","Senior Research Fellow"]},{"type":"h","text":"8+ years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Lead","Research Programme Director","Senior Academic/Research Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For BA Buddhist / Islamic / Christian / Jain / Comparative Religion Studies → Researcher, the strongest pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Religious Studies","One Deep Specialisation","Research Methods","Relevant Classical/Regional Language","Digital Humanities","Academic Writing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The key is to avoid remaining a generalist with only broad knowledge of religions. Choose one primary research area—such as Buddhist Studies, Islamic Studies, Christian Studies, Jain Studies, religion and society, religious texts, interfaith relations, or digital religion—and build a substantial research portfolio around it."},{"type":"p","text":"For a long-term academic or specialist research career, a relevant master's followed by doctoral research is usually the strongest progression, while students who combine religious studies with data, digital humanities, languages, or policy research can access a broader range of modern research roles."}]}]}